<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suvarnagiri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suvarnagiri, 'golden mountain', was a city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, named in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a>'s minor rock edicts as the seat of a prince who governed the southern province. Many scholars identify it with Kanakagiri in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, near the gold-bearing country around Maski where Ashokan edicts have been found. It was one of the four provincial capitals of the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suvarnagiri.jpg" alt="Suvarnagiri" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dineshkannambadi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Kanakachalapathi_temple_at_Kanakagiri_in_the_Koppal_district.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
